---
import ArticleLayout from "@layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
import VideoShowcase from "@components/VideoShowcase.astro";
import { bellingenShowcase } from "../../data/bellingen-destination";
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="Bellingen Destination"
  description="A destination website concept for Bellingen, bringing local places, events and community together."
  eyebrow="Selected work / Website"
  subtitle="A welcoming digital home for Bellingen."
  tags="Web design · Destination"
  backHref="/work/"
  backText="← Back to selected work"
>
  <VideoShowcase slot="art" {...bellingenShowcase} />

  <section>
    <h2>A destination, at a glance.</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      A website concept for Bellingen that brings the region’s landscapes, local
      places, events and community into one clear destination.
    </p>
    <p>
      The home page opens on a waterfall and a welcome to Bellingen. From there,
      visitors can explore featured listings and events, learn about the
      community, and find ways to connect.
    </p>
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/assets/bellingen-destination/1.jpg"
        width="2250"
        height="1500"
        loading="lazy"
        alt="Bellingen website homepage showcase, with a waterfall behind the Welcome to Bellingen heading."
      />
      <figcaption class="caption">
        A welcoming introduction to the destination.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>A guide to local food.</h2>
    <p>
      The “Where to eat” page gives local listings a clear, browsable home. A
      featured introduction leads into a grid of places, with links to explore
      more of the region.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Space for individual places.</h2>
    <p>
      The Cedar Bar page shows how a local business can have its own place in
      the wider destination. Practical details sit alongside a photo gallery and
      related listings.
    </p>
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/assets/bellingen-destination/2.jpg"
        width="2250"
        height="1500"
        loading="lazy"
        alt="Angled collage of Bellingen website designs showing the waterfall homepage, community section and Cedar Bar venue page."
      />
      <figcaption class="caption">
        A connected visual system for the destination, community and local
        places.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Community at the centre.</h2>
    <p>
      The landscape introduces the destination; the people give it character. A
      dedicated community section brings the region’s creative life and local
      stories into the experience.
    </p>
    <figure>
      <img
        src="/assets/bellingen-destination/3.jpg"
        width="1620"
        height="1620"
        loading="lazy"
        alt="Bellingen website detail pairing the waterfall homepage with a community introduction and local photography."
      />
      <figcaption class="caption">
        Landscape and community, brought together in one welcoming experience.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <a class="text-link" href="/work/">
    Explore more selected work ↗
  </a>
</ArticleLayout>

<style>
  img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .article-prose figure {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
  }
  .caption {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
</style>
